From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d, d3d11: stream output appends at the buffer's filled size; DrawAuto

A Direct3D stream output buffer has a filled size (BufferFilledSize):
SOSetTargets with an offset of -1 goes on where the buffer's last stream
output stopped -- also after the buffer was unbound -- and DrawAuto draws as
many vertices as that size holds at the vertex buffer's stride. wined3d's
OpenGL renderer wrote every append from the start of the buffer
("Appending to stream output buffers not implemented") and DrawAuto, of
both d3d10 and d3d11, was a stub that drew nothing: GPU particle systems and
other multi-pass stream output rendered nothing or garbage when Vulkan (and
so DXVK) is not there and wined3d's OpenGL path is the fallback.

Each transform feedback session counts what it writes per stream
(GL_TRANSFORM_FEEDBACK_PRIMITIVES_WRITTEN, indexed per stream); the buffers
written keep the count with where the writes started and the bytes per
primitive (stride times the primitive's vertices), and the filled size is
resolved only when asked for: binding with -1, or a draw with
wined3d_device_context_draw_auto() (new), whose vertex count is taken when
the draw runs from the buffer at vertex input slot 0 (filled size less the
binding offset, over the stride). An application's own primitives-written
query on the same stream cannot run beside it: that session is then not
counted (FIXME). wined3d's Vulkan renderer: DrawAuto and appending are not
done (FIXME); Vulkan machines use DXVK. Multiple vertex streams stay
unsupported (d3d11 refuses them: "Streams not implemented yet").

Gate: test/d3d11soauto-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_SO_NO_FILLED_SIZE).
